.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt ADIADC 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm adiadc
.Nd finite receive sessions for an ADI AXI ADC
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "ad9361phy* at spi?"
.Cd "adiaxidmac* at fdt?"
.Cd "adiaxiadc* at fdt?"
.In dev/fdt/adi_axi_adc.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
interface provides exclusive, receive-only access to an AD9361 converter
and its FIFO-to-memory DMA channel.
It implements finite captures, not a continuous recording service.
The device node is owned by root with mode 0600.
Only one session can open a converter at a time.
.Pp
Open the device with
.Dv O_RDONLY .
The interface has no write or memory mapping operation.
Transmit controls are absent.
The converter must have an explicit receive-only FDT policy.
The current character interface requires 1R1T mode with physical RX1.
A two-receiver configuration remains available to kernel consumers.
.Sh IOCTLS
Every request must specify
.Dv ADI_AXI_ADC_ABI_VERSION
and the exact structure size.
Initialize reserved request fields to zero.
.Bl -tag -width ADI_AXI_ADCIOC_CAPTURE
.It Dv ADI_AXI_ADCIOC_CONFIG
Configure frequency, sample rate, analog bandwidth, RF input and gain.
Use
.Dv ADI_AXI_ADC_RX1_MASK
and
.Dv ADI_AXI_ADC_RX1_IQ_CHANNEL_MASK .
Gain and RSSI use millidecibel units.
This request invalidates the previous capture.
The first configuration initializes RX clocks after safe DMA admission.
A change to frequency alone preserves the sampling clocks and tuned link.
Hardware-specific range limits can be narrower than the ABI limits.
.It Dv ADI_AXI_ADCIOC_CAPTURE
Arm a finite capture with a sample count and a timeout.
The first subsequent
.Xr read 2
starts DMA.
The buffer must hold the complete capture.
A short initial read fails before DMA starts.
The count must produce an eight-byte aligned transfer of at most one MiB.
.It Dv ADI_AXI_ADCIOC_STATUS
Return the session state, captured count, capture error and fresh RX status.
A configured or armed session is not a completed capture.
Check status after reading all samples.
Only entries selected by valid_mask have RSSI and gain data.
.El
.Pp
Each complex sample contains two little-endian 16-bit words: I, then Q.
Each word holds a signed 12-bit sample in bits 11 through 0.
These samples do not provide calibrated RF power in dBm.
.Sh DMA OWNERSHIP
A capture retains its buffers until DMA completion and a positive drain witness.
The exact no-SG DMAC 4.5.c reset-manager debug state is supported.
Missing debug state or a drain timeout prevents release and poisons the session.
Unknown hardware requires a supported external drain provider.
DMA safety does not establish RF settling, capture continuity
or antenna performance.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/adiadc0
.It Pa /dev/adiadc0
First finite receive device.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width EOPNOTSUPP
.It Er EBUSY
Another session owns the converter.
.It Er EINVAL
Invalid ABI, topology, count, timeout or configuration.
.It Er EOPNOTSUPP
The hardware or drain operation is unsupported.
.It Er ETIMEDOUT
Capture or hardware drain exceeded its deadline.
.It Er EIO
A hardware failure poisoned the session.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr fdt 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
interface was added to EmberBSD in October 2026.
